# SC4MP chat panel. Packed into sc4mp-dll-ui.dat by tools/make-ui-dat.py; the control ids must match ChatPanel.cpp.
# The frames and most buttons are the game's own images, used by their keys like its dialogs do: the steel frame {46a006b0,144161ee} stretched as an
# edge image and its caption button {46a006b0,144161eb}, with its fonts and text color.
# Its top window isn't moveable by the game (moveable=no), since the DLL drags it by its title band: the game's own moving, by the
# window's edge, fought with it and made it jump.
# The chat lines scroll with the game's own scrollbar (GZWinScrollbar with {46a006b0,46a006a6}, as in its bridge picker), which the DLL sets and
# hit-tests itself, since the panel keeps its clicks from the map. A hint (0x7B3E9A6C, 0x7B3E9A6D) counts new messages below while scrolled up.
# The title has most of the title band, so long server names fit. The save status is an icon before the buttons, with its text as the tooltip of a
# see-through button over it (0x7B3E9A90), set by the DLL. The panel is either open or minimized to the chip: a round button
# like the game's (eg. {46a006b0,cbcb6e9b}, drawn at 50 pixels), with the status as its ring's colour, a globe cut out of the game's {46a006b0,14416310}
# (chat-globe.png) as a button on it, and the unread count on a red bubble.
# The other images are drawn by tools/make-ui-images.py, at the size of the windows that show them. Windows are drawn in the order they're listed.
# The panel can be resized by its bottom corners, and the DLL moves and stretches the windows here, which are laid
# out for its default size of 8 rows. Rows 8 to 15 are for a taller panel and start hidden. The text field (0x7B3E9A68, and 0x7B3E9A69 while
# typing) is an edge image, so the game stretches it to the field's width and keeps its rounded ends.
# Each chat line has a text window in the game's text color (0x7B3E9A70 + row), a grey one for lines that aren't chat (0x7B3E9AB0 + row), and a window for the player's name in each of
# the launcher's name colors (0x7B3E9B00 + row * 0x10 + color), since the pinned gzcom-dll has no way to change a text window's color. The colors must match kNameColors in ChatPanel.cpp.
<LEGACY clsid=GZWinGen iid=IGZWinGen id=0x7B3E9A60 area=(8,64,374,298) fillcolor=(0,0,0) caption=" " winflag_visible=yes winflag_enabled=yes winflag_moveable=yes winflag_sizeable=no winflag_sortable=no winflag_pbuff=no winflag_pbufftrans=yes winflag_pbufferase=yes winflag_pbuffvid=no winflag_alphablend=yes winflag_acceptfocus=no winflag_mousetrans=no winflag_ignoremouse=no userdata=0 moveable=no sizeable=no defaultkeys=no closevisible=no gobackvisible=no minmaxvisible=no closedisabled=no gobackdisabled=no minmaxdisabled=no titlebar=no fill=no outline=no paint=yes sidebar=no gutters=(4,4) >
